cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or its data, please cite the manuscript given under preferred-citation."
type: software
title: "PoreVoronoi-FV"
abstract: >-
  Code, case inputs and result records of the manuscript "PoreVoronoi-FV: Conservative pore-scale flow on cells
  fixed by tracked particles". PoreVoronoi-FV is a finite-volume Stokes-flow method on cells around
  particle-visited voxels: each voxel goes to the nearest of them through the pore, so every cell is one
  connected piece. Code: Apache-2.0; data: CC BY 4.0 except where DATA_LICENSE.md states otherwise.
authors:
  - family-names: Zhu
    given-names: Linqi
    email: linqi.zhu@imperial.ac.uk
    affiliation: "Department of Earth Science and Engineering, Imperial College London; I-X, Imperial College London"
repository-code: "https://github.com/LinqiZhu/PoreVoronoi_FV"
license:
  - Apache-2.0
  - CC-BY-4.0
keywords:
  - finite volume method
  - Stokes flow
  - geodesic Voronoi diagram
  - particle tracking velocimetry
  - data assimilation
  - local mass conservation
